1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,002
Most businesses use a few
other tools alongside Kyntlo.

2
00:00:04,002 --> 00:00:07,885
In this lesson, you'll connect
them directly from a workflow.

3
00:00:07,885 --> 00:00:12,405
We'll receive data with an inbound
webhook, add rows to a Google Sheet,

4
00:00:12,405 --> 00:00:14,506
and send data out to another app.

5
00:00:15,358 --> 00:00:17,064
These are premium features.

6
00:00:17,064 --> 00:00:22,183
They're included on the Pro plan, and each
time a premium trigger or action runs,

7
00:00:22,183 --> 00:00:24,015
a small usage charge applies.

8
00:00:24,015 --> 00:00:27,617
You'll find the current rates
on the Kyntlo pricing page.

9
00:00:27,617 --> 00:00:30,334
In the builder, look
for the premium badge.

10
00:00:31,184 --> 00:00:32,436
Here's the example.

11
00:00:32,436 --> 00:00:35,401
Bloom's website is built
on another platform,

12
00:00:35,401 --> 00:00:38,234
and its enquiry form
needs to reach Kyntlo.

13
00:00:38,234 --> 00:00:43,571
Every enquiry should become a contact,
and a row in the practice manager's Google

14
00:00:43,571 --> 00:00:43,966
Sheet.

15
00:00:44,816 --> 00:00:46,759
The trigger is Inbound Webhook.

16
00:00:46,759 --> 00:00:48,889
Kyntlo gives you a unique address.

17
00:00:48,889 --> 00:00:53,777
Copy it, and paste it into your other
app, as the place to send new enquiries.

18
00:00:54,627 --> 00:00:59,501
Then send one test enquiry from that
app, and click Fetch sample requests.

19
00:00:59,501 --> 00:01:03,979
Kyntlo shows the data it received:
name, email, phone and treatment.

20
00:01:03,979 --> 00:01:07,075
Now it knows which fields
are available to map.

21
00:01:07,930 --> 00:01:13,231
The first action, Create Contact, maps
that incoming data onto contact fields.

22
00:01:13,231 --> 00:01:18,872
The first name, email and phone from the
webhook become a real contact in your CRM,

23
00:01:18,872 --> 00:01:21,794
with tags so you know
where they came from.

24
00:01:22,644 --> 00:01:23,887
Next, Google Sheets.

25
00:01:23,887 --> 00:01:28,426
Connect your Google account once, then
choose what to do: create, update,

26
00:01:28,426 --> 00:01:29,918
look up or delete a row.

27
00:01:29,918 --> 00:01:32,343
Pick the spreadsheet and the worksheet.

28
00:01:33,329 --> 00:01:36,987
Then map each column in your
sheet to a custom value.

29
00:01:36,987 --> 00:01:41,612
Name goes in the name column, email
in the email column, and so on.

30
00:01:41,612 --> 00:01:45,063
Every new enquiry adds a
fresh row, automatically,

31
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:47,410
so the sheet is always up to date.

32
00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:48,514
Save the action.

33
00:01:49,369 --> 00:01:51,635
Data can travel the other way too.

34
00:01:51,635 --> 00:01:53,901
Click plus and search for webhook.

35
00:01:53,901 --> 00:01:57,632
The standard Webhook action
posts contact data to a URL.

36
00:01:57,632 --> 00:02:02,164
Custom Webhook is the premium
version, where you control the method,

37
00:02:02,164 --> 00:02:05,896
headers and body, for tools
that need a specific format.

38
00:02:06,744 --> 00:02:09,572
Enter the address your
other tool gave you,

39
00:02:09,572 --> 00:02:13,123
check the body uses the right
custom values, and save.

40
00:02:13,123 --> 00:02:17,661
Now every enquiry is also sent to
that system, the moment it arrives.

41
00:02:18,512 --> 00:02:23,514
You'll find a few more premium actions
in the list, such as Custom Code,

42
00:02:23,514 --> 00:02:26,779
and the AI actions, like
GPT Powered by OpenAI.

43
00:02:26,779 --> 00:02:29,211
We'll use those in the next module.

44
00:02:30,063 --> 00:02:31,124
Here's a pro tip.

45
00:02:31,124 --> 00:02:36,241
When you connect another tool, send one
test record, and then open Execution Logs.

46
00:02:36,241 --> 00:02:39,548
You'll see exactly what was
sent, and what came back,

47
00:02:39,548 --> 00:02:42,232
before real customer
data flows through it.

48
00:02:43,081 --> 00:02:46,042
Your workflows can now
talk to your other tools.

49
00:02:46,042 --> 00:02:50,855
In the final lesson of this module,
you'll learn to troubleshoot any workflow,

50
00:02:50,855 --> 00:02:53,569
using enrollment history
and execution logs.

51
00:02:53,569 --> 00:02:54,433
See you there!
